# Whitelist, not blacklist: this repo root holds `.env*` with live credentials,
# the host-side `.data/uploads` tree (candidate CVs and pitch recordings), a real
# CV pdf, `node_modules` and prompt scratch. A blacklist would have to name every
# one of them and would silently ship the next thing added. Everything is
# excluded, then only what `next build` reads is let back in.
#
# The load-bearing exclusion is `.env*`: Next inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at build
# time, so a build that reads the host's `.env.local` bakes live credentials
# into an image layer that survives in the build cache. Nothing has to be inlined
# any more — the browser only ever talks to the origin it was served from, and
# server-side link building reads `APP_URL` at runtime (docker/app/Dockerfile:26).
# So the build takes no credential-carrying ARGs at all.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!next.config.ts
!next-env.d.ts
!tsconfig.json
!eslint.config.mjs
!AGENTS.md
!src
!public
!scripts
!docker/app/Dockerfile
